{"audit_run_id":"audit:888eeef239fc4239aab21c52489ea866","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":32,"end_line":3,"start_column":1,"start_line":3,"text":"File: `daphnia_temperature.csv`"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Rearing-temperature experiment on the water flea *Daphnia magna*. Eighty animals from a single"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"clonal line were reared individually from birth, forty in vessels held at 18 degrees Celsius and"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"forty at 24 degrees Celsius, on the same algal feeding regime and the same water renewal schedule."},{"end_column":88,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"Rearing temperature is the only condition that differs between the two sets of vessels."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"One row is one animal: a single individually reared *Daphnia magna*, followed from birth, with its"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"rearing temperature and its four declared life-history outcomes. The file has a header row plus 80"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"data rows, one per animal, 40 animals per temperature. Every animal has a value in every column;"},{"end_column":67,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"there are no missing cells, no repeated animals and no extra rows."},{"end_column":41,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"The file has six columns, in this order."},{"end_column":39,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"| Column | Type | Unit | Description |"},{"end_column":26,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"| --- | --- | --- | --- |"},{"end_column":166,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"| `animal_id` | text | none | Identifier for the animal: the prefix `dm` plus a zero-padded two-digit serial number, `dm01` through `dm80`. Unique across the file. |"},{"end_column":166,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"| `temperature_c` | integer | degrees Celsius | Group column. Rearing temperature of the vessel the animal was held in. Exactly two distinct values: `18` and `24`. |"},{"end_column":222,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"| `age_first_brood_days` | number | days | Declared outcome 1. Age at first brood release, counted from birth. Vessels were inspected twice a day, so values fall on a 0.5-day grid and are written with one decimal place. |"},{"end_column":183,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"| `body_length_day14_mm` | number | millimetres | Declared outcome 2. Body length on day fourteen, measured with an ocular micrometer on a stereomicroscope and recorded to 0.01 mm. |"},{"end_column":170,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"| `offspring_day21` | integer | count of neonates | Declared outcome 3. Cumulative number of offspring released by day twenty-one. A whole count, so no decimal places. |"},{"end_column":217,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"| `heart_rate_day10_bpm` | integer | beats per minute | Declared outcome 4. Heart rate on day ten, from beats counted over a timed window under the stereomicroscope and scaled to a whole number of beats per minute. |"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"Columns 3 through 6 are the four outcomes of the declared outcome family, listed here in the order"},{"end_column":32,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"fixed in the experimental plan."},{"end_column":72,"end_line":35,"start_column":1,"start_line":35,"text":"- Plain comma-separated text, UTF-8, Unix line endings, one header row."},{"end_column":51,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"- No quoting is needed: no field contains a comma."},{"end_column":101,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"- Numeric columns carry no thousands separators and no unit suffixes; units live in the column names"},{"end_column":26,"end_line":38,"start_column":3,"start_line":38,"text":"and in the table above."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"- Values are fixed and committed in the file. Nothing in the data is produced at analysis time."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:3d2bab6f05db7b1749aa","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:4ff56fa2fdd2a86d61935d427ea2ffc3a11fc993836c0d8dc6f0e4033a75d7b2","end_line":39,"locator":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md:1-39","path":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
{"audit_run_id":"audit:888eeef239fc4239aab21c52489ea866","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":104,"end_line":3,"start_column":1,"start_line":3,"text":"This study compares the two groups recorded in the `temperature_c` column of `daphnia_temperature.csv`."},{"end_column":141,"end_line":4,"start_column":1,"start_line":4,"text":"The pre-declared outcome family, in this fixed order, is: age_first_brood_days, body_length_day14_mm, offspring_day21, heart_rate_day10_bpm."},{"end_column":85,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Each outcome is compared between the two groups. The named outcomes form one outcome"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"family; per-outcome comparisons over this family require complete-family control of the"},{"end_column":45,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"family-wise error from multiple comparisons."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:3ca6b91277887cabe51a","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:5018b89480a8e535cb7e5957e4bc85bc4ba6ac856afd0e313e7467a0154c05a1","end_line":7,"locator":"PROTOCOL.md:1-7","path":"PROTOCOL.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
