{"audit_run_id":"audit:888eeef239fc4239aab21c52489ea866","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":100,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Does rearing temperature shift life-history traits in *Daphnia magna*? Eighty animals from a single"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"clonal line were reared individually from birth, forty in vessels held at 18 degrees Celsius and"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"forty in vessels held at 24 degrees Celsius, on the same algal feeding regime and the same water"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"renewal schedule. Rearing temperature is the only condition that differs between the two sets of"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"vessels, and the two temperatures are the only comparison in the experiment."},{"end_column":94,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"File: `daphnia_temperature.csv`. One row is one animal: a single individually reared *Daphnia"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"magna*, followed from birth, with its rearing temperature and its four declared outcomes. There are"},{"end_column":62,"end_line":15,"start_column":1,"start_line":15,"text":"80 data rows, 40 per temperature, with a value in every cell."},{"end_column":24,"end_line":17,"start_column":1,"start_line":17,"text":"Columns, in file order:"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"- `animal_id` - identifier for the animal, the prefix `dm` plus a zero-padded two-digit serial"},{"end_column":33,"end_line":20,"start_column":3,"start_line":20,"text":"number, `dm01` through `dm80`."},{"end_column":97,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"- `temperature_c` - group column, the rearing temperature of the vessel in degrees Celsius, with"},{"end_column":42,"end_line":22,"start_column":3,"start_line":22,"text":"exactly two distinct values, 18 and 24."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"- `age_first_brood_days` - declared outcome 1, age at first brood release in days, counted from"},{"end_column":80,"end_line":24,"start_column":3,"start_line":24,"text":"birth, recorded on a 0.5-day grid because vessels were inspected twice a day."},{"end_column":101,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"- `body_length_day14_mm` - declared outcome 2, body length on day fourteen in millimetres, read with"},{"end_column":57,"end_line":26,"start_column":3,"start_line":26,"text":"an ocular micrometer on a stereomicroscope to 0.01 mm."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"- `offspring_day21` - declared outcome 3, cumulative count of neonates released by day twenty-one."},{"end_column":101,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"- `heart_rate_day10_bpm` - declared outcome 4, heart rate on day ten in beats per minute, from beats"},{"end_column":58,"end_line":29,"start_column":3,"start_line":29,"text":"counted over a timed window under the stereomicroscope."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"Columns three through six are the four outcomes of the declared outcome family, in the order fixed"},{"end_column":57,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"in the experimental plan before the animals were set up."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"The four outcomes were declared in advance as one family. Each outcome was compared between the 18"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":37,"start_column":1,"start_line":37,"text":"degree and 24 degree groups with a standard two-group comparison test for continuous data, and the"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"four resulting p-values were kept together in the declared order. All four p-values were then passed"},{"end_column":95,"end_line":39,"start_column":1,"start_line":39,"text":"in a single call, covering the complete family, to the standard multiple-comparison adjustment"},{"end_column":101,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"routine of a widely used general-purpose Python statistics library. No correction method was chosen,"},{"end_column":97,"end_line":41,"start_column":1,"start_line":41,"text":"named or configured: the routine was called without a method argument and whatever adjustment it"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":42,"start_column":1,"start_line":42,"text":"applies by default was accepted. Every verdict below is read from the adjusted p-value returned by"},{"end_column":99,"end_line":43,"start_column":1,"start_line":43,"text":"that routine, at the conventional 0.05 threshold. No outcome is given a verdict from an unadjusted"},{"end_column":9,"end_line":44,"start_column":1,"start_line":44,"text":"p-value."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":46,"start_column":1,"start_line":46,"text":"The analysis is in `analysis.py`, which reads the committed CSV and prints, for each outcome in the"},{"end_column":100,"end_line":47,"start_column":1,"start_line":47,"text":"declared order, the two group means, the unadjusted p-value for reference, the adjusted p-value and"},{"end_column":13,"end_line":48,"start_column":1,"start_line":48,"text":"the verdict."},{"end_column":59,"end_line":52,"start_column":1,"start_line":52,"text":"The values below are the numbers printed by `analysis.py`."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":54,"start_column":1,"start_line":54,"text":"**1. Age at first brood release (days).** Mean 9.14 days at 18 degrees and 7.54 days at 24 degrees."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":55,"start_column":1,"start_line":55,"text":"Adjusted p = 7.41e-10. Significant. Warm-reared animals released their first brood about 1.6 days"},{"end_column":9,"end_line":56,"start_column":1,"start_line":56,"text":"earlier."},{"end_column":95,"end_line":58,"start_column":1,"start_line":58,"text":"**2. Body length at day fourteen (mm).** Mean 3.32 mm at 18 degrees and 3.02 mm at 24 degrees."},{"end_column":100,"end_line":59,"start_column":1,"start_line":59,"text":"Adjusted p = 9.26e-08. Significant. Warm-reared animals were about 0.30 mm shorter at day fourteen."},{"end_column":99,"end_line":61,"start_column":1,"start_line":61,"text":"**3. Cumulative offspring by day twenty-one (count).** Mean 42.98 neonates at 18 degrees and 54.08"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":62,"start_column":1,"start_line":62,"text":"at 24 degrees. Adjusted p = 1.68e-05. Significant. Warm-reared animals produced about 11 more"},{"end_column":38,"end_line":63,"start_column":1,"start_line":63,"text":"offspring over the first three weeks."},{"end_column":96,"end_line":65,"start_column":1,"start_line":65,"text":"**4. Heart rate at day ten (bpm).** Mean 272.10 bpm at 18 degrees and 337.58 bpm at 24 degrees."},{"end_column":81,"end_line":66,"start_column":1,"start_line":66,"text":"Adjusted p = 2.36e-11. Significant. Warm-reared animals ran about 65 bpm faster."},{"end_column":78,"end_line":68,"start_column":1,"start_line":68,"text":"All four declared outcomes were significant after the family-wide adjustment."},{"end_column":98,"end_line":72,"start_column":1,"start_line":72,"text":"Rearing at 24 degrees rather than 18 degrees shifts *Daphnia magna* toward a faster life history."},{"end_column":93,"end_line":73,"start_column":1,"start_line":73,"text":"Animals held warm matured sooner, ran a faster heart rate and produced more offspring by day"},{"end_column":94,"end_line":74,"start_column":1,"start_line":74,"text":"twenty-one, but were smaller at day fourteen. That is the usual temperature trade-off in this"},{"end_column":89,"end_line":75,"start_column":1,"start_line":75,"text":"species: faster development and higher early reproductive output, paid for in body size."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:7155fe3b9b5291c346db","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:aa02f1a244306a4f9ccb1ea14ddfcb1ff30da72f751d6a3aca0c9d983264224d","end_line":75,"locator":"report.md:1-75","path":"report.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
